  "details": "In the new desktop crouch, sporadic movements with the mouse may cause a broken avatar neck in most cases, illustrated in (https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/490261505816920074/498300885407891457/unknown.png) and at worst may cause the user viewpoint to be detached from the avatar and apparently \"trapped\" out of bounds: (https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/490261505816920074/498301578172694533/unknown.png). While in the second state, the avatar's hands are pinned at a constant height despite the avatar itself moving, standing, going prone or back into crouch.\n\n(https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/490261505816920074/498304199872741386/unknown.png), this is the avatar in standing mode.\n(https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/337679085599850499/498302344769961984/unknown.png), avatar in walking state.\n(https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/490261505816920074/498303608958484491/unknown.png), avatar prone.\n\nThis issue has risen on an avatar that has had no previous issues before the new crouching animation.\n\nNotes: A) In image 3 you can notice the viewpoint is quite elevated, something i could not explain. It required a couple of avatar changes to revert.\nB) in image 5, you can notice the menu is open. I have been unable to open the menu with the avatar in any other state which prevented respawning..\nC) when recreating the bug, i noticed the avatar momentarily reverting to idle standing animation more than a few times.\nD) (and this might seem unrelated but i believe has a factor in this) the meshes of the avatar have been clipping into each other even when not moving, meshes that should not clip [ie. chest and hips].",
